<%# jscpd duplication (DRY) gate config — CANON-22 Tier-1 (Juergens et al. ICSE'09).
    `threshold` is a CEILING (% duplicated tokens); the debt ratchet additionally
    enforces monotonic non-increase (Lehman's law of rising entropy). Juergens'09:
    INCONSISTENT clones — a fragment duplicated then edited in one copy but not the
    other — are the dangerous ones (latent bugs), so minTokens is kept low to surface
    near-duplicates rather than only exact copies. Threshold scales with governance.
    jscpd v5 ignores the v4 `pattern` key (silent 0-file scan): the fileset lives in
    `path` (read by the generated scripts and passed as positional CLI args — jscpd
    itself disregards the key) plus the `format` filter. -%>
{
  "threshold": <%= duplicationThreshold %>,
  "minTokens": 50,
  "reporters": ["json", "consoleFull"],
  "absolute": true,
  "path": ["src"],
  "format": ["typescript", "tsx", "javascript", "jsx"],
  "ignore": [
    "**/node_modules/**",
    "dist/**",
    "build/**",
    "coverage/**",
    "**/__tests__/fixtures/**",
    "**/*.min.js"
  ]
}
